  "deletedBy": null,
  "details": "I am unsure if this is known already but many accounts that are made on VRChat are scammer and/or bot accounts which find groups with Discord links and click to join them from the VRChat website. These scammers/bots then wreak havoc on unprepared servers by flooding them with illegitimate accounts and they then message members and attempt to scam them by offering to make them avatars. They often do not ever make the avatars or they contract someone else on Fiverr/elsewhere to make the avatar and they take a steep middleman tax by overcharging the scammed VRChat user.\n\nIt is very apparent from the links that I have posted in my own group that these scammer/bots are only coming from VRChat and often from Visitor user ranks. \n\nTherefore, I propose that someone needs to be of a certain trust rank to be able to click and access the link. I propose that someone must need to be at least a User rank to be able to click Discord or other website links and the links be \"greyed out\" and unable to be linked to or seen before then.\n\nI propose that someone be at least New User rank but, preferably, User rank before being able to click any social media links. \n\nThank you for considering this proposal.",
